n the last 18 years and ~3x the bank's own 10-year CAGR.\n- Rated AA- (Stable) by India Ratings.\n- RAM (Retail, Agriculture, MSME) advances remain the core focus, at 94.33% of Gross Advances.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Regulatory/Legal] Two Enforcement Directorate Show Cause Notices remain live: SCN1 (2014, share-transfer contraventions) saw its ₹17 crore penalty reduced to ₹3.40 crore on appeal, with the bank to receive ₹13.60 crore back and ED's share-confiscation claim dismissed, while a share-transfer regularisation application is pending with RBI; SCN2 (2017, bonus-share issuance) has a proposed ₹1,037 crore penalty still under adjudication, which management's legal advice pegs the real exposure at ₹2 lakh (fully provided).\n- [Accounting transition] Expected Credit Loss (ECL) norms effective 01.04.2027 create a one-time additional provision requirement of ₹385 crore, against which ₹304.24 crore of provisions (₹54.24 crore upfront ECL provisioning plus a ₹250 crore existing contingency provision) is already available.\n- [Shareholding] Mutual Fund and Foreign Portfolio Investor holdings both rose YoY (MF 0.000%→0.663%, FPI 4.654%→6.859% between 30.09.2025 and 30.09.2026), while Public holding declined correspondingly.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}]},"sources":["investor presentation 26-10-2026","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"Tamilnad Mercantile Bank positions itself as a RAM-focused (Retail/Agri/MSME) private bank growing well above industry pace while holding asset quality, capital adequacy and collateral coverage strong, with Total Business up 27.25% YoY.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":6.17,"fy":"FY26","mcap":9979,"opm":74.1,"pe":7.5,"roe":14.0}],"wtt":null},"drhp":{"rpt":{"financials":{"_source":"ledger","balance_sheet_key":[{"basis":"Standalone","fy":"FY2023","total_assets_amount_rs":5789536000